Source: nvidia-open-kernel-@arch@-signed
Section: gpu/kernel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Pexip AS <packaging@pexip.com>
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Standards-Version: 4.3.0
Build-Depends: debhelper (>= 10.1~),
 linux-kbuild-@kabi@,
 nvidia-open-kernel-unsigned-@kabi@-@arch@ (= @version_binary@),

Package: nvidia-open-kernel-@kabi@-@arch@
Architecture: @arch@
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
Built-Using: nvidia-open-gpu-kernel-modules (= @version_binary@)
Description: NVIDIA signed open kernel modules
 This package provides a pre-built binary of the NVIDIA binary kernel modules.
 .
 The NVIDIA binary driver provides optimized hardware acceleration of
 OpenGL/GLX/EGL/GLES applications via a direct-rendering X Server
 for graphics cards using NVIDIA chip sets.
 .
 This package is built for linux-image-@kabi@.
